<title>HUNGARY: CESI index weakens, ends at 1,468.67 points.</title>
<headline>CESI index weakens, ends at 1,468.67 points.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index fell 1.04 percent or 15.46 points to 1,468.67 points on Wednesday, the Budapest Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index, as a result of its regular review, reflects trends of 72 Hungarian, Polish, Czech, Slovak and Slovenian shares since May 2, instead of 73 shares before.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
